# Aether — recognised environment variables
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` (gitignored) as a record of your local
# overrides. The shell auto-loads `.env.local` from the repo root at
# main-process startup via `shell/electron/main/env-loader.ts` (and
# raven-core loads the same file via `daemons/raven-core/raven_core/
# config.py:_load_dotenv`), so values set below flow into `process.env`
# for everything the shell spawns — Core, mesh nodes, daemons.
#
# Precedence: env vars already set in your shell (export'd in ~/.zshrc,
# or via direnv, or passed on the command line) win over `.env.local`.
# That means `.env.local` is for per-machine defaults; transient
# overrides still work via the command line without editing this file.
#
# Anything not listed here uses the resolver / built-in default — there is
# no value below that is required for the shell to boot.
#
# Per-machine values only: secrets that need to survive reboot (none in
# v0.1.0 — the shell regenerates fresh hex-32 secrets per cold start)
# will move to the system keychain in a future PR
# (MASTER_SYNTHESIS.md §7 Q6). Don't put real production secrets here.

# ---- Voice (raven) ----------------------------------------------------------
# The only key most setups ever need. Voice is the single capability that
# requires it — the shell boots fine without one (the mic button reports
# voice unavailable). Loaded by raven-core via the same .env.local.
#
# GEMINI_API_KEY=<your-gemini-api-key>

# ---- Python resolution -----------------------------------------------------
# Skip the login-shell `command -v python3` lookup the shell does at boot.
# Save 50-200ms of cold-start latency by pointing directly at the python3
# binary that has aiohttp, pyyaml, and jsonschema installed. See
# core/README.md → "Locating python3" for resolution order.
#
# MESH_PYTHON=/opt/homebrew/bin/python3
# MESH_PYTHON=/usr/local/bin/python3
# MESH_PYTHON=/Library/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/3.14/bin/python3

# ---- Core URL (for nodes spawned outside the shell) -----------------------
# When the shell spawns a node, it sets MESH_CORE_URL to point at the Core
# it just brought up — you do not need to set this for the normal `pnpm
# dev` flow. Override only if running a node manually against a Core you
# started by hand (e.g. `cd core && python3 -m core.core …`).
#
# MESH_CORE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000

# ---- Node data dir (for nodes spawned outside the shell) -------------------
# nodes that persist state (news_feeds → SQLite) need a writable root.
# The shell hands them HOMEOS_DATA_DIR pointing at <userData>/data; when
# running a node by hand, point this anywhere writable. The node creates
# its own subdirectory under this root (e.g. news_feeds/news.db).
#
# HOMEOS_DATA_DIR=/tmp/homeos-data

# ---- Finance node ---------------------------------------------------------
# The finance node requires no API key as of v0.3.x. It fetches from
# Yahoo Finance (primary, via the `yahoo-finance2` npm) with a Stooq
# CSV fallback when Yahoo flakes — both anonymous endpoints, no env
# var to set. See DECISIONS.md "Second data node: finance" for the
# provider-swap rationale.

# Weather node (Open-Meteo, no auth required)
AETHER_WEATHER_LAT=37.7749
AETHER_WEATHER_LON=-122.4194
AETHER_WEATHER_LABEL=San Francisco

# ---- GitHub node (the gap board) -------------------------------------------
# Lets Aether file, read, and comment capability-gap issues on the live
# GitHub issue board (nodes/github). Without a token the node serves a
# clean degraded payload — the shell and every other capability run fine.
#
# AETHER_GITHUB_TOKEN — a fine-grained PAT scoped to Issues read/write on
# the target repo. Never logged.
# AETHER_GITHUB_REPO  — optional target override; defaults to
# ashwinsreedhar28/Aether.
#
# AETHER_GITHUB_TOKEN=<fine-grained-PAT>
# AETHER_GITHUB_REPO=<owner/repo>

# ---- Music node (Spotify playback) ------------------------------------------
# Lets Aether drive Spotify playback (nodes/music): play / pause / skip /
# queue / search plus the now_playing sensor surface. Without a client id the
# node boots degraded — every surface denies music_no_client_id by name; the
# shell and every other capability run fine.
#
# SPOTIFY_CLIENT_ID — from your Spotify developer app
# (https://developer.spotify.com/dashboard). The app MUST register the
# redirect URI http://127.0.0.1:8898/callback. No client secret — auth is
# Authorization Code with PKCE; the browser grant runs once on the first
# actor call and the refresh token is cached owner-only under the node's
# data dir. Playback control needs Spotify Premium.
#
# SPOTIFY_CLIENT_ID=<your-spotify-client-id>

# ---- Calendar node (macOS only) --------------------------------------------
# The calendar node reads events from macOS Calendar.app via EventKit.
# On first invocation macOS prompts the user for Calendar access permission.
# No env vars to configure — permission is managed via System Settings →
# Privacy & Security → Calendar. If permission is denied, all three surfaces
# return {available: false, reason: 'permission_denied'}.

# Reminders node (macOS Reminders.app via EventKit)
# No env vars required. Reminders.app permission required on first daemon
# spawn; grant via the macOS prompt or System Settings → Privacy & Security
# → Reminders → toggle Aether.
# System info node (battery, disk, network, active app)
# No env vars required. Uses macOS native shell commands.
# Active app detection requires Automation access for System Events
# (System Settings → Privacy & Security → Automation), granted on first prompt.
